level 3:
elevator · module !1,3
  on board · list
  Elevator · record ● ← changed by simulator
  stops · set
  State · state ● ? ← changed by Elevator, simulator

externals
output.csv · csv file

state machines
machine State (in elevator): states going up, door open, stopped, going down
  ? initial state not declared
  going up → door open: simulator
  door open → stopped: simulator
  stopped → going up: Elevator
  stopped → door open: simulator
  stopped → going down: Elevator
  going down → door open: simulator

roles (what the primitives presuppose)
Config · configuration: source=config; validation=config
floors traveled · metric: definition=sum of floors of all elevators
mean trip · metric: definition=alighting minus boarding
mean wait · metric: definition=boarding minus arrival
nearest, round robin, zone · strategy: input=candidates, floor; output=Elevator, None
wait p95 · percentile: method=nearest rank; definition=?
arrivals · poisson process: rate=rate
now · clock: unit=s
event queue · priority queue: order=simulated time; tie-breaker=scheduling order
per-floor rng · random generator: seed=origin floor, seed
STRATEGIES · registry: contents=nearest, round robin, zone

invariants and rules
!1 If the record "Elevator" is full, the module "simulator" skips the record "Elevator".
!2 If the module "simulator" does not serve the record "Passenger", the module "simulator" raises the error "RuntimeError".
!3 If the set "stops" contains the value "called floor", the module "simulator" skips the list "waiting".
!4 If the module "config" raises the error "ValueError", the command "run" exits with the value "2".
!5 If the strategy "zone" returns the value "None", the module "simulator" skips the list "waiting".
!6 When the field "floors" changes, the random generator "per-floor rng" changes the list "passengers".
!7 If the field "floors" is greater than 36, the report "timeline" prints the value "?".
∀ Every strategy in the registry "STRATEGIES" returns the value "None".
∀ Every strategy in the registry "STRATEGIES" receives the value "floor".
∀ Every strategy in the registry "STRATEGIES" returns the record "Elevator".
∀ Every strategy in the registry "STRATEGIES" receives the list "candidates".

gaps (the description does not say), warnings and absences (none, on purpose)
⚠ field “speed”: the name suggests q.speed (distance/time), but the unit 's/floor' is time/distance
? percentile “wait p95”: missing definition
? state machine “State”: missing initial state
∅ field “seed”: no limit, on purpose
